    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as the undisputed anchor of the lineup, boasting an elite 83.29 efficiency score. His matchup against Freddy Peralta is prime for production; beyond the favorable 4.35 xERA, the combination of a significant park boost and a slow delivery from Peralta creates a high-upside environment for **Gunnar Henderson** to utilize his wheels on the basepaths. Behind him, **Kyle Tucker** (74.88) and **Andy Pages** (74.11) offer robust secondary value. Both benefit from a soft matchup against Bubba Chandler, with **Andy Pages** specifically positioned to exploit Chandler's slow delivery, maximizing our focus on securing stolen bases in a tight 5x5 race.\n\nThe optimizer faced its toughest decision at the utility spot, ultimately rewarding **Coby Mayo** (59.94) over **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (45.16). While **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** offers utility, he struggled against the projected L/L dynamic platoon disadvantage against Mason Fluharty, dropping him well below the viability threshold. Conversely, **Coby Mayo** capitalized on the hitter-friendly park factors and a solid order placement, barely edging out the rest of the bench. We are tracking a 37% rain risk for the games involving **Miguel Vargas** and **Luis Robert Jr.**; both players are currently in the lineup, but we will monitor the situation closely, especially given **Luis Robert Jr.**\u2019s already dampened efficiency score due to the R/R matchup against Sean Burke.",
